svyashchennaya-kniga-name = sacred book
svyashchennaya-kniga-desc = A heavy folio bound in pale leather, smelling of incense and myrrh. Between the canonical lines and across the broad margins, dreadful brown notes have been scratched by a priest's trembling hand.
svyashchennaya-kniga-content = [head=3]The Testaments of Soma, Lifegiver and Mother of Flesh[/head]


    {"1. I am Soma, the Font of every breath. Set no other hope before thee in the hour of grief and weakness, for in My palm lies hidden the seed of healing."}

    {"[color=#8a0303][italic](In the margin:)[/italic] I 6elieved in the M0ther 0f Fle5h, and n0w I 5ee a mercile55 m0n5ter... We 6egged Her t0 5ave u5 fr0m the ~reature, and 5he *heard.[/color]"}


    {"2. All flesh is sacred, and the human life is the vessel of My grace. Spill not thy brother's blood in wrath, nor leave thy neighbor rotting in his wounds."}

    {"[color=#8a0303][italic](Between the lines:)[/italic] Th1s pl4gue is n0t a sickne55, but Her twisted gift. 5he c0mmanded the Fle5h t0 bl00m...[/color]"}


    {"3. If thou seest the leper and the sorely suffering, turn not thy face away. Lay thy hands upon his wounds, wash them with the tear of mercy, and death shall retreat."}

    {"[color=#8a0303][italic](Written straight over the text:)[/italic] 5he d0es n0t heal! 5he d0es n0t let u5 d1e! Death w0uld be great mercy, but 50ma t00k it fr0m u5...[/color]"}


    {"4. Raise life where decay has cast its seed. Stand against corruption, that flesh may bloom in My glory, for life is eternal and knows no bounds."}

    {"[color=#8a0303][italic](Crookedly scratched along the side:)[/italic] N0w the Fle5h bl00ms wild, mad, kn0wing n0 b0und5. 50res split 0pen 0n 0ur b0dies like black fl0wers... A man has bec0me n0 m0re than a bed f0r r0tting meat...[/color]"}


    {"5. I command you, priests and healers: bear comfort unto every border. Where pain reigns, there shall My love abide, and where flesh suffers, there shall life triumph."}

    {"[color=#8a0303][italic](At the bottom of the page, in bloodstains:)[/italic] L1fe triump5... I c0ugh bl00d, and in that bl00d pul5es the seed 0f Her \"grace\". F0rgive u5... eternal life in the Fle5h is true hell...[/color]"}

dnevnik-samuraya-name = diary of a "samurai"
dnevnik-samuraya-desc = A leather notebook, clearly brought from distant western lands. Inside, in uneven, sweeping handwriting, the author has recorded his attempts to grasp eastern wisdom. The pages are heavily stained with green tea rings and candle wax.
dnevnik-samuraya-content = [bold]Day 1.[/bold]

    {"Arrived at my new home in the bamboo grove. Gods, everything is so austere! No bulky oak furniture, just woven mats on the floor. I told the local governor [bold]ARIGATO[/bold], bowed just as that blind monk taught me, and with trembling hands hung my katana on its wooden stand. From this day forth, I live by the code of [bold]BUSHIDO[/bold]. My path to enlightenment begins!"}


    {"[bold]Day 3.[/bold]"}

    {"My lower back is begging every western god for mercy. Who even invented sleeping on a hard floor with a wooden log under your head instead of a proper feather pillow?! My neck has seized so badly that I can only look east."}


    {"This morning I tried drinking their bitter green tea. There are no proper clay mugs here! Only a tiny teapot and bowls the size of quail eggshells. By the time I had enough, I nearly died of thirst from pouring boiling water again and again. I went into the yard and said [bold]KONNICHIWA[/bold] to a flowering bush. It said nothing. It must be absorbing the spirit of zen."}


    {"[bold]Day 6.[/bold]"}

    {"At the roadside market I bought a fine, juicy haunch of pork. I brought it home, already dreaming of a warrior's hearty supper, and then cold sweat struck me. [bold]THERE IS NO OVEN HERE.[/bold] None at all! No stone hearth, no spit, not even a miserable little fire! How do these cursed island aesthetes eat meat at all?! Their kitchen has only a thin carving knife, an empty table, and a kettle!"}


    {"In desperation, I tried roasting the pork by skewering it on my katana and holding it over three candles on the nightstand. For two hours I smoked up the room, made the whole house stink of paraffin, and finally ate a half-raw piece that tasted of wax. The honor of the samurai has cracked."}


    {"[bold]Day 8.[/bold]"}

    {"My stomach twists so fiercely that I am near to committing ritual [bold]SEPPUKU[/bold] right in the middle of this cursed tea room. I sit on the tatami, staring at the carving knife and the raw meat. If no wandering trader comes by before evening to sell me a normal cooking pot and a sack of turnips, I shall shout [bold]BANZAI[/bold] and devour this haunch raw, like a wild goblin."}


    {"[bold]SAYONARA[/bold], my healthy stomach. You served me faithfully."}

    {"[color=#555555]░▒▓██▒░ The mat smells of despair ░▒▓████████[/color]"}

