skomkannyy-pergament-name = crumpled parchment
skomkannyy-pergament-content = [head=3]Complaint to the Magistrate![/head]


    {"[italic]A copy has been sent to the director of this so-called \"troupe\".[/italic]"}


    {"I demand the immediate return of my three silver coins! What you had the gall to present to me as \"high theatrical art\" proved to be the lowest sort of fairground farce, pitched in the middle of forest mud."}


    {"Firstly, your vaunted stalls are nothing but roughly hewn wooden benches! I drove a splinter into my finest velvet breeches while trying to settle upon that instrument of torture. Secondly, why must the honorable public knead the slush with their boots merely to reach the auditorium? Could you not have laid even a little straw along those paths?!"}


    {"And the performance itself! It was laughable! Your actor playing Bright Soma forgot his lines, tripped over a cardboard tree on the stage, and stank so fiercely of fermented ale that no perfume could save him. The musician in the left dressing room missed every note on his clattering banjo, and those stone \"thrones\" on the stage look as though they were dragged in from the nearest graveyard. I shall say nothing of that ridiculous horn, blown at entirely the wrong moments."}


    {"[color=#8b0000][bold]This is not a theater. This is a pigsty![/bold][/color]"}


    {"If my money is not delivered to the inn by tomorrow morning, I shall see to it that the guard closes your farce for offending public morals and committing fraud!"}


    {"[italic]Master Waldemar, connoisseur of the fine arts.[/italic]"}

izyashchnyy-pergament-name = elegant parchment
izyashchnyy-pergament-content = [head=3][color=#800000]A Woodland Mystery[/color][/head]


    {"[italic]Enthusiastic verses from a grateful spectator[/italic]"}


    {"Deep in the wood, where treetops sigh,"}

    {"A wondrous hall was raised on high."}

    {"Though thrones were crude and carved of pine,"}

    {"The spirit of art there still did shine!"}


    {"Upon the stage, the Sun and Moon"}

    {"Renewed their ancient starry tune."}

    {"And strings rang clear through forest air,"}

    {"With voices lifted bright and fair."}


    {"The playful banjo brightly rang,"}

    {"The horn into the heavens sang."}

    {"Such living art, so strange and grand,"}

    {"Made every watcher stand still!"}


    {"Forgetting benches hard and mean,"}

    {"And midnight chill beneath the green,"}

    {"We cast our coins with open hands"}

    {"In candlelight upon those lands!"}


    {"[bold]Praise to the actors! Bravo to the masters![/bold]"}

nadushennyy-pergament-name = perfumed parchment
nadushennyy-pergament-desc = A thick, expensive sheet of paper with a faint scent of lilac and gooseberry. The handwriting is elegant and swift, each letter flawlessly even, yet every stroke carries unmistakable, haughty irritation.
nadushennyy-pergament-content = [head=3][color=#4b0082]Private Notes[/color][/head]


    {"I had the highly questionable pleasure of passing through the so-called Holy Land of our dear Church. A charming place, of course, if one happens to enjoy the smell of cheap incense, unwashed bodies, and fanatical stupidity."}


    {"The priests of Bright Soma, with their pompously grave faces, sell \"sanctified\" amulets right by the gates. Out of pure professional curiosity, I deigned to test one such trinket for an arcane field. Astonishing. An ordinary roadside cobblestone possesses more magical potency than this piece of painted wood. Yet the pilgrims continue crawling through the mud on their knees in rapture, buying this trash for full-weight gold."}


    {"They call it divine grace and a higher design. I call it an excellently arranged pyramid scheme and mass hysteria. No descent of divine light, nor even the poorest excuse for an aura, can be observed in these lands. I did, however, discover a most powerful source of unsanitary conditions."}


    {"I shall leave this blessed place at the first opportunity. I sincerely hope that by the time I reach a respectable inn, this unbearable smell of righteousness will have aired out of my robe."}


    {"- Merlin Temnova"}

